  "details": "Summary\n\nI would like to suggest a feature that allows users to control who can see their own avatar based on other users' Trust Ranks.\n\nThis setting should control the visibility of the user's avatar to others, rather than which avatars the user can see.\n\nProposed Features\n\n1. Avatar Visibility Settings by Trust Rank\n\nAllow users to choose which Trust Ranks are permitted to see their avatar.\n\nFor example:\n\nVisitor\n\nNew User\n\nUser\n\nKnown User\n\nTrusted User\n\nUsers should be able to independently allow or restrict avatar visibility for each Trust Rank.\n\n2. Individual User Visibility Settings\n\nAllow users to set whether their own avatar is visible to specific individuals, regardless of the general Trust Rank settings.\n\nEach individual should have the following options:\n\nFollow the general Trust Rank visibility settings (default).\n\nAlways allow this user to see my avatar.\n\nNever allow this user to see my avatar.\n\nThis would make it possible to manage exceptions without changing the general settings.\n\n3. Default Settings and First-Time Notification\n\nI suggest allowing all Trust Ranks to see users' avatars by default.\n\nWhen users first launch VRChat after this feature is introduced, a brief notification should explain the new settings and how to configure them.\n\nBenefits\n\nHelps protect users' avatars from unwanted access by potential bot accounts.\n\nGives avatar creators greater control over who can see their creations.\n\nAllows users to restrict avatar visibility without unnecessarily excluding legitimate new users.\n\nProvides flexible management through both global Trust Rank settings and individual exceptions.\n\nConclusion\n\nI believe this feature would improve avatar security and give users greater control over the visibility of their own avatars.\n\nThe goal is to provide better protection while maintaining a welcoming and accessible social environment for everyone.\n\nThank you for considering this suggestion!",
